## Commands
- `atmos fix`: apply every automatic fix (deprecated syntax, unused declarations, formatting, managed files, README). Breaking for module interfaces; review the diff.
- `atmos lint`: validate only. Never changes files.
- `atmos test`: run `tests/*.tftest.hcl` against the emulator; real AWS only via `atmos auth`.
- `atmos docs generate readme`: rebuild `README.md` from `README.yaml`.

## Rules
- Do not hand-edit `README.md`, `context.tf` (copied from terraform-null-label by the scaffold), or anything marked "Managed by the terraform-module scaffold".
- Every variable and output has a type and a description. No unused variables, outputs, or providers.
- AWS provider constraint is `>= 6.0` with an explicit `source`. Pin module sources to a registry version or git ref.
- Tests live in `tests/` as `*.tftest.hcl` with enabled and disabled cases. No Makefiles, bats, or Terratest.
- A breaking change needs the `major` label and `docs/migration-vX-to-vY.md`.
- Never run `apply` against real AWS without a stated reason.

